---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Screenshot from '../components/Screenshot.astro';
---
<Layout title="A closer look" description="Explore QiRing's encrypted Ring, password profiles, offline password-health report, recovery, and portable mode. See the real interface with fictional demo data.">
  <section class="shell page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Inside QiRing</p><h1>A home for the things<br />you need to remember.</h1><p class="lede">A focused desktop app for the everyday work of keeping credentials organized. No online account required.</p></section>
  <section class="shell showcase"><div class="showcase-copy"><span class="mini-number">01 / UNLOCK YOUR RING</span><h2>Your Ring.<br />Your way in.</h2><p>Open QiRing and unlock your existing Ring with your master password. Your credentials stay on your computer, with no online account to sign in to.</p><p>If you forget your master password, your saved recovery key lets you set a new one. Keep that key somewhere safe and separate from your computer.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/unlock/">Learn about unlocking & recovery ↗</a></div><Screenshot name="unlock" alt="QiRing unlock screen with an empty master-password field and recovery-key option for a fictional demo Ring" caption="A simple welcome back to your Ring." eager /></section>
  <section class="shell showcase reverse"><div class="showcase-copy"><span class="mini-number">02 / YOUR RING</span><h2>Everything together.<br />Easy to find.</h2><p>Keep logins and private notes in a searchable, categorized Ring. Add tags, images, custom fields, and security questions without scattering the details across different tools.</p><p>Store a TOTP setup key alongside a login to generate its six-digit code locally. Passwords and secret fields stay masked until you choose to reveal them.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/vault/">Read the Ring & Qi editor guide ↗</a></div><Screenshot name="ring" alt="Fictional Juniper Mail login selected in the categorized QiRing workspace" caption="One Qi, with its details together." /></section>
  <section class="shell showcase"><div class="showcase-copy"><span class="mini-number">03 / PASSWORD PROFILES</span><h2>A good password.<br />On your terms.</h2><p>Save the rules you actually need: length, uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, allowed symbols, and whether to avoid ambiguous characters.</p><p>Test a profile before saving it, then reuse it whenever you generate a password for a Qi.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/profiles/">Build your first profile ↗</a></div><Screenshot name="profiles" alt="QiRing password profile editor showing the fictional demo's Strong 20 generation rules" caption="Save a policy. Generate a fresh password." /></section>
  <section class="shell showcase reverse"><div class="showcase-copy"><span class="mini-number">04 / RING HEALTH</span><h2>A useful check-in.<br />Entirely offline.</h2><p>Review weak, reused, and older passwords without sending passwords or hashes to a network service. Jump from a finding directly to the entry that needs attention.</p><p>This is a local password-quality review. It does not search online breach databases.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/health/">Understand the health report ↗</a></div><Screenshot name="health" alt="QiRing's offline health report with findings for fictional demo entries" caption="A clear view of what needs a little care." /></section>
  <section class="section shell"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Made for the everyday</p><h2>The little things<br />matter, too.</h2></div><p>Choose how QiRing fits into your desktop, and make a plan for keeping your Ring safe.</p></div><div class="feature-editorial"><article><h3>A way back in.</h3><p>A mandatory recovery ceremony helps you record and verify your recovery key. Recovery rotates the key and sets a new master password.</p><a href="/guide/unlock/" class="text-link">Recovery explained ↗</a></article><article><h3>A copy when you need it.</h3><p>Export an encrypted backup with a separate passphrase, keep local snapshots, or preview and map a CSV import.</p><a href="/guide/backups/" class="text-link">Backups & transfer ↗</a></article><article><h3>Your desktop, your rhythm.</h3><p>Light and dark themes, keyboard shortcuts, auto-lock settings, clipboard timing, and portable Linux and Windows builds.</p><a href="/guide/settings/" class="text-link">Make it yours ↗</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="shell cta-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">See it for yourself</p><h2>Start with a little test Ring.</h2><p>Every screenshot on this site uses fictional data. Try the same approach while you explore the prerelease.</p></div><a class="button" href="/downloads/">Choose your download ↓</a></section>
</Layout>
